{
  "esm": "1.2.0",
  "metadata": {
    "name": "process-refueling-runspec",
    "description": "PLAN.md §7.5 step 7d: the `process-refueling` RunSpec computed from the DEFAULT DATABASE. It mounts `moves-onroad.esm` -- the 74 national tables and the onroad model -- and supplies the run's own selections and its expected output.\n\nIT IS A CHAINED CALCULATOR WITH NO RATE OF ITS OWN. `RefuelingLossCalculator` scales the Total Energy Consumption a vehicle burned: REFEC-1 and REFEC-2 turn the hour's temperature and the month's fuel supply into grams of vapour per gallon, REFEC-3 to REFEC-6 apply the onboard-recovery penetration and the Stage II program reduction, and REFEC-7 divides the energy by kilojoules-per-gallon to get the gallons. In this chain that is a RATIO to the parent, exactly as SO2 and CO2 are: `rt_refuelingChainRatio` is the loss rate over (energy content x fuel density), and `lnk_weight` carries the kilojoule-to-MillionBTU rebase every energy-to-mass edge needs (conventions §77).\n\nTHE TWO BLOCKS ARE DIFFERENT SIZES, 64 and 104, and the two suppressions are different joins. `refuelingControlTechnology` carries fuel types 1 and 5 only, so diesel has no displacement rate row at all -- 40 diesel cohorts are in the spillage block and absent from the displacement one. Electricity is dropped from BOTH by REFEC-7, because `fuelSubtype.energyContent` is NULL for subtype 90 and `fuelType.fuelDensity` is NULL for fuel type 9 and the extract keeps only rows where both are positive. It is NOT the rate that drops electricity: `sourceTypeTechAdjustment` knows nothing about fuel, so the spillage side HAS a row for every electricity cohort with a rate of zero. A document that dropped them on the rate would agree here on all 168 rows and be wrong the first time a fuel had a spill rate and no energy content.\n\nWHAT IT COST THE MODEL, beyond the calculator itself, was two corrections to gates that seventeen earlier RunSpecs had agreed with.\n\nFIRST, A ROAD TYPE. `emissionProcess.occursOnRealRoads` is 'N' on both refueling processes and MOVES emits them at road type 4. The flag says where `BaseRateGenerator` WRITES a process's rates, and it writes none for 18 or 19 -- neither rate table carries a single row at either, measured on the national database. A chained calculator's rows are stamped on their parent's, so they take the parent's road type. Off-network processes 2, 90 and 91 do have rate rows and keep road type 1, which is what `expand-day` depends on, so the corrected rule changes nothing there.\n\nSECOND, AND IT IS THE FIRST TIME THE EXECUTION DATABASE IS NOT ENOUGH. `runspecpollutantprocess` carries seven rows and MOVES emits two. Three of the seven are Total Energy Consumption, which `ExecutionRunSpec.flagRequiredPollutantProcesses` ADDED -- the RunSpec asked for hydrocarbons at the two refueling processes and nothing else -- and the output processor strips what it added. The execution database records the EXPANDED set and not the user's, and the XML that records the user's is the file this repository has a rule against reading. What makes it recoverable anyway is that the needs table is REFUELING-ONLY: thirty rows, five pollutants crossed with the two refueling processes, each requiring Total Energy Consumption at running, start and extended-idle exhaust, and no other calculator in MOVES adds a prerequisite at all. So `rspp_isSilentlyRequired` derives the strip from the selections plus a declared table, and it has exactly one blind spot: `require()` does not flag a pair the user had already selected, so a RunSpec asking for refueling AND for energy would keep its energy block where this chain drops it. No run in the corpus does that, and the document says so rather than leaving it to be found.\n\nIT EMITS 168 ROWS and computes 250 more it does not emit. `n_outputRate` is 168, `cohortSurvivorCount` is 104 -- not the 125 the energy spine carries -- and the shape check recomputes both.",
    "authors": [
      "EarthSciML Authors and Contributors"
    ],
    "tags": [
      "fixture",
      "onroad",
      "default-database",
      "refueling"
    ]
  },
